          "line": 65,
          "severity": "P3",
          "title": "BROWSERLESS_TOKEN not restored after test, pollutes shared process env",
          "text": "🟢 **P3**\n\n**BROWSERLESS_TOKEN not restored after test, pollutes shared process env**\n\nThis test sets `process.env.BROWSERLESS_TOKEN = 'test-token'` but never restores or deletes it after the test runs (no `afterEach` cleanup for this variable). Since `afterEach` in this file only restores `globalThis.fetch` and calls `mock.reset()`, the env var leaks into subsequent tests within this file and potentially into other test files run in the same Node process. Any later test that expects `BROWSERLESS_TOKEN` to be unset (to exercise the UNCONFIRMED-without-token path) could get a false pass/fail depending on execution order, since only the first test in this suite explicitly saves/restores the original value."
        },
